# Battery Supply Chain Risk Intelligence Platform — Admin Dashboard Build

## How to use this file
Place this file at the root of the Next.js frontend project as `.cursorrules`.
It provides persistent context for every Cursor session on this project.

---

## Project Overview

You are building the admin dashboard and v1 product interface for a B2B supply chain risk intelligence platform. The platform ingests data about EV battery supply chains, scores companies on risk across six pillars, and generates PDF/HTML reports for clients.

This frontend is the **internal admin tool first** (for data verification and report generation) and becomes the **client-facing SaaS product** later. Build everything as if it is already the product — same auth, same patterns, same API design. The only difference between admin and client is the Clerk role.

The first client deliverable is **reports**, not a live dashboard. The report generation flow is the most important UX to get right.

---

## Existing Backend

The FastAPI backend lives in a separate repository (`battery-data-intelligence-engine`). It is already built with:
- SQLAlchemy ORM with Alembic migrations
- Neon Serverless Postgres database
- All schema tables created and seeded
- CLI-based scoring engine (six pillars, v3.0)
- No API routes yet — you are building them

**You are building:**
1. FastAPI API routes in the existing backend repo
2. A new Next.js 14+ frontend (App Router) in a separate `/frontend` directory or repo

---

## Tech Stack — Do Not Deviate

### Frontend
- **Next.js 14+** with App Router and TypeScript
- **Tailwind CSS** for styling
- **shadcn/ui** for base components (buttons, tables, dialogs, badges, cards, inputs, selects, tabs)
- **shadcn/ui charts** for all data visualization (bar charts, area charts, pie charts — built on Recharts, React 19 compatible). KPI cards use shadcn/ui Card. Do NOT install Tremor — it does not support React 19.
- **Clerk** for authentication (already has `clerk_org_id` and `clerk_user_id` in DB schema)
- **TanStack Query (React Query v5)** for server state, data fetching, and caching
- **React Hook Form + Zod** for forms and validation
- **Axios** for HTTP client to FastAPI

### Backend additions (in existing FastAPI repo)
- **Pydantic v2** response models for all new routes
- All routes versioned under `/api/v1/`
- CORS configured for Next.js origin
- Clerk JWT verification middleware for protected routes

---

## Database Schema — Key Tables

All tables are in Neon Postgres. The FastAPI ORM models already exist. You are building API routes on top of them.

### Companies
```
companies: id (UUID), canonical_name, legal_name, supply_chain_stage
           (oem|cell_maker|miner|refiner|recycler|holding),
           headquarters_country, headquarters_region, public_ticker,
           is_public, parent_company_id (self-ref UUID), data_confidence (0-1),
           data_source, notes

company_aliases: id, company_id, alias, alias_type

company_material_exposures: id, company_id, material_id, supply_chain_stage,
                            exposure_score (0-1), source_geography (ISO2),
                            data_confidence, rationale, as_of_date

company_supply_relationships: id, buyer_id (→companies), supplier_id (→companies),
                              material_id, relationship_type (direct|indirect|estimated),
                              data_confidence, volume_share_pct (0-1), valid_from, valid_to

company_regulation_exposure: id, company_id, regulation_id,
                             compliance_status (compliant|non_compliant|partial|unknown),
                             exposure_reason, assessed_at

company_vehicle_models: id, company_id, model_name, model_year_start,
                        model_year_end, production_volume_units,
                        production_volume_year, is_active

vehicle_model_chemistries: id, vehicle_model_id, battery_chemistry_id,
                           share_pct (0-1), valid_from, valid_to, notes
```

### Scoring
```
company_scores: id, company_id, as_of_date,
                material_concentration_risk_score, geopolitical_trade_risk_score,
                regulatory_risk_score, operational_risk_score,
                financial_pressure_score, overall_risk_score,
                supply_chain_propagation_score, scoring_version,
                rationale_json (JSONB)

rationale_json shape:
{
  "inputs": { "scoring_version": "3.0", "run_id": "...", "evidence_window_days": 365 },
  "components": {
    "material": float, "geopolitical": float, "regulatory": float,
    "operational": float, "financial": float,
    "supply_chain_propagation": float | null, "overall": float
  },
  "top_evidence": [event_ids],
  "decay": { "eval_date": "YYYY-MM-DD", "operational_half_life": 90 },
  "notes": "human-readable string — ALWAYS display this to users",
  "propagation_chain": [...],
  "chemistry_mix": [...],
  "signals_used": { ... }
}
```

### Risk Intelligence
```
risk_events: id, event_type, event_date, title, summary,
             severity_score (0-1), confidence_score (0-1),
             risk_categories_json, geography_json, content_hash

regulations: id, regulation_key, title, issuing_body, geography,
             policy_theme, status, publication_date, effective_date, summary

materials: id, canonical_name, category, criticality_score (0-1),
           is_ira_critical_mineral (bool), is_eu_crma_critical (bool),
           data_availability

hs_material_mappings: id, hs_code (str, 6–10 digits, HS-2017 or HS-2022 vintage),
                      material_id (→materials), hs_description, mapping_confidence (0-1),
                      mapping_source (manual|inferred|external_dataset),
                      hs_revision (e.g. "HS2022"), notes,
                      created_at, updated_at
                      // Used to translate trade-flow HS codes into canonical materials.
                      // Multiple HS codes may map to one material; one HS code should
                      // map to at most one material per (hs_revision).

facilities: id, company_id, facility_type, country, city, status,
            capacity_notes, latitude, longitude
```

### Platform
```
tenants: id (UUID), clerk_org_id, name, plan (starter|pro|enterprise)
users:   id (UUID), tenant_id, clerk_user_id, email, role (owner|admin|analyst|member)

report_templates: id, org_id, name, focus_type, audience_type,
                  is_platform_template, weight_overrides (JSONB), sections_config (JSONB)
report_runs:      id, org_id, template_id, report_type, audience_type,
                  as_of_date, status (queued|running|completed|failed), parameters_json
report_insights:  id, report_run_id, insight_type, title, body,
                  related_company_id, related_material_id, related_regulation_id,
                  sort_order, metadata_json

analyst_notes:    id, entity_type (company|material|regulation|geography|risk_event),
                  entity_id (string), note_type, note_text, created_at
```

