## FastAPI Routes to Build

Build these routes in the existing backend. All routes require Clerk JWT verification
except health check. Admin-only routes additionally require role check.

### Response conventions
- All list endpoints return: `{ "data": [...], "total": int, "page": int, "limit": int }`
- All detail endpoints return the resource directly
- Errors return: `{ "error": str, "detail": str }`
- Dates as ISO strings, UUIDs as strings

### Companies
```
GET    /api/v1/companies
       Query params: page, limit, search, stage, country, parent_id, min_confidence
       Returns paginated company list with: id, canonical_name, legal_name,
       supply_chain_stage, headquarters_country, data_confidence,
       latest_score (overall_risk_score + band), parent_company_name

GET    /api/v1/companies/{id}
       Returns full company detail including aliases and parent info

GET    /api/v1/companies/{id}/exposures
       Returns company_material_exposures with material canonical_name joined

GET    /api/v1/companies/{id}/relationships
       Returns both directions: as_supplier (buyer_name, material, volume_share)
       and as_buyer (supplier_name, material, volume_share)

GET    /api/v1/companies/{id}/regulations
       Returns company_regulation_exposure with regulation title, policy_theme,
       effective_date joined

GET    /api/v1/companies/{id}/events
       Query params: limit (default 20), event_type
       Returns risk_events linked via risk_event_companies, ordered by event_date desc

GET    /api/v1/companies/{id}/facilities
       Returns all facilities for company

GET    /api/v1/companies/{id}/vehicle-models
       Returns company_vehicle_models with vehicle_model_chemistries
       and battery_chemistry slug joined

GET    /api/v1/companies/{id}/score
       Returns latest company_scores row with full rationale_json
       Query param: as_of_date (optional, defaults to latest)

GET    /api/v1/companies/{id}/score/history
       Returns all company_scores rows ordered by as_of_date desc
       for trend display

POST   /api/v1/companies/{id}/notes
       Body: { note_type: str, note_text: str, entity_type: "company" }
       Creates analyst_notes row. Returns created note.

GET    /api/v1/companies/{id}/notes
       Returns all analyst_notes for this company ordered by created_at desc
```

### Notes / Flag-Issue Pattern (generalized in Phase 2)

Phase 1 only supports flagging companies. Phase 2 generalizes the same
pattern to every reference-data entity so analysts can flag bad seed data
on materials, HS-code mappings, regulations, risk events, facilities, and
chemistries.

**Per-entity routes (mirrors the company pattern — keep REST consistent):**
```
POST   /api/v1/materials/{id}/notes
GET    /api/v1/materials/{id}/notes
POST   /api/v1/materials/{material_id}/hs-mappings/{mapping_id}/notes
GET    /api/v1/materials/{material_id}/hs-mappings/{mapping_id}/notes
POST   /api/v1/regulations/{id}/notes
GET    /api/v1/regulations/{id}/notes
POST   /api/v1/risk-events/{id}/notes
GET    /api/v1/risk-events/{id}/notes
POST   /api/v1/facilities/{id}/notes
GET    /api/v1/facilities/{id}/notes
POST   /api/v1/chemistries/{id}/notes
GET    /api/v1/chemistries/{id}/notes
```

**Shared body shape (Pydantic):**
```python
class AnalystNoteBase(BaseModel):
    note_type: Literal["data_error", "missing_data", "outdated", "other"]
    note_text: str = Field(min_length=3, max_length=4000)

class AnalystNoteCreate(AnalystNoteBase):
    # Each per-entity route hardcodes entity_type from the URL prefix and
    # entity_id from the path param — clients must NOT send them. The
    # server writes them into analyst_notes.entity_type / entity_id.
    pass

class AnalystNoteRead(AnalystNoteBase):
    id: int
    entity_type: Literal[
        "company", "material", "hs_material_mapping",
        "regulation", "risk_event", "facility", "battery_chemistry",
    ]
    entity_id: str  # always serialized as string (UUIDs and ints both)
    created_at: datetime
```

The frontend exposes a single `EntityFlagIssueDialog` that accepts an
`entityType` + `entityId` + the URL template for the matching POST/GET
routes — see `components/shared/entity-flag-issue-dialog.tsx`.

### Scores
```
GET    /api/v1/scores
       Query params: page, limit, band (LOW|MOD|HIGH|CRIT), stage,
                     sort_by (overall|material|geopolitical|regulatory|
                              operational|financial|propagation),
                     sort_dir (asc|desc), as_of_date
       Returns company scores with company name and stage joined.
       Band logic: LOW 0-34, MOD 35-54, HIGH 55-74, CRIT 75-100
```

### Scoring Engine
```
POST   /api/v1/scoring/run                        [admin only]
       Body: { company_ids?: string[], as_of_date?: string }
       Triggers rescore. If company_ids empty, runs all.
       Returns: { run_id: str, status: "queued", company_count: int }
       Runs the existing rescore_all CLI logic asynchronously via BackgroundTasks.

GET    /api/v1/scoring/runs                       [admin only]
       Returns last 20 scoring runs with status, company_count, started_at, completed_at

GET    /api/v1/scoring/runs/{run_id}              [admin only]
       Returns run status. Poll this after triggering a run.
       Returns: { run_id, status, companies_scored, errors, started_at, completed_at }
```

### Reports
```
POST   /api/v1/reports/generate
       Body: {
         template_id?: string,
         company_ids: string[],
         report_type: string,       // "supplier_risk" | "regulatory" | "material_concentration"
         audience_type: string,     // "internal" | "oem" | "investor" | "public"
         as_of_date: string,
         title?: string
       }
       Creates report_run row with status=queued.
       Triggers report generation via BackgroundTasks.
       Returns: { report_id: int, status: "queued" }

GET    /api/v1/reports
       Query params: page, limit, status, report_type
       Returns report_runs list with org context

GET    /api/v1/reports/{id}
       Returns report_run with all report_insights ordered by sort_order

GET    /api/v1/reports/{id}/download
       Returns signed R2 URL (or generates PDF from insights if R2 not yet configured)
       Short TTL (15 min). Do not store URL in DB.
```

### Reference Data (read-only, except notes)
```
GET    /api/v1/materials
       Query params: page, limit, search, category, is_ira_critical,
                     is_eu_crma_critical, has_mismatched_mappings (bool)
       Returns paginated MaterialListItem with: id, canonical_name, category,
       criticality_score, is_ira_critical_mineral, is_eu_crma_critical,
       data_availability, hs_mapping_count (int), mapping_mismatch_count (int)

GET    /api/v1/materials/{id}
       Returns MaterialDetail with criticality_signals and chemistry_uses,
       plus a top-level ``hs_mappings: HsMaterialMappingRead[]`` array
       (all mappings for the material, latest revision first) and a
       ``mapping_health: { total: int, mismatched: int, low_confidence: int,
       missing_description: int }`` summary block.

       "Mismatched" detection criteria (server-side):
         - mapping_confidence < 0.6, OR
         - hs_description is NULL/empty, OR
         - HS chapter (first 2 digits of hs_code) does NOT match the
           material's canonical category (e.g. lithium → HS chapter 28),
         - OR more than one material maps to the same hs_code within the
           same hs_revision (cross-mapping check, returned as a flag on
           every offending row).

GET    /api/v1/materials/{id}/hs-mappings
       Query params: hs_revision, mapping_source, min_confidence
       Returns HsMaterialMappingRead[] for one material (used by the
       Mappings tab on the detail page; same data as MaterialDetail.hs_mappings
       but filterable in isolation).

GET    /api/v1/hs-mappings/mismatches
       Query params: page, limit, severity (low|medium|high)
       Returns a global list of suspected bad HS↔material mappings, joined
       with material canonical_name. Powers the "Mismatches" view that the
       /data/materials list links to.

GET    /api/v1/regulations
       Query params: page, limit, search, status, policy_theme,
                     issuing_body, effective_after

GET    /api/v1/regulations/{id}
       Returns regulation with material_scope and geography_scope joined

GET    /api/v1/risk-events
       Query params: page, limit, event_type, severity_min, date_from, date_to,
                     search

GET    /api/v1/facilities
       Query params: page, limit, company_id, country, facility_type, status,
                     search

GET    /api/v1/chemistries
       Query params: page, limit, search
       Returns battery_chemistries with latest chemistry_risk_scores joined
```

### Admin-Only Routes
```
POST   /api/v1/admin/ingestion/run               [admin only]
       Body: { source: str, params?: dict }
       Triggers ingestion for a specific source.

GET    /api/v1/admin/ingestion/runs              [admin only]
       Returns ingestion_runs ordered by started_at desc

GET    /api/v1/admin/seed-review                 [admin only]
       Query params: seed_type, status
       Returns seed_review_findings
```

