## Key Component Patterns

### DataTable (reusable across all list pages)
Use TanStack Table v8 with shadcn/ui Table primitives.
Every list page uses this component. Columns are defined per-page as columnDefs.
Built-in: sorting, pagination (server-side), row click navigation.
Toolbar slot for filters and search — each page passes its own filter controls.

```tsx
<DataTable
  columns={companyColumns}
  data={companies}
  total={total}
  page={page}
  limit={limit}
  onPageChange={setPage}
  onRowClick={(row) => router.push(`/companies/${row.id}`)}
  toolbar={<CompanyTableToolbar filters={filters} onFiltersChange={setFilters} />}
/>
```

### Score Badge
```tsx
// score → band → color
// 0-34:  LOW      → green  badge
// 35-54: MODERATE → amber  badge
// 55-74: HIGH     → orange badge
// 75-100: CRITICAL → red   badge
<ScoreBadge score={72} />  // renders "HIGH 72"
```

### Pillar Breakdown (on company score page)
Use shadcn/ui BarChart (horizontal). Six bars labeled with pillar name, weight, and score.
Show actual score (0-100) not the weighted contribution.
Color bars by score level (green < 35, amber < 55, orange < 75, red >= 75).
Import from `@/components/ui/chart` — this is the shadcn/ui chart primitive, not a third-party package.

### Rationale Card
The most important component for evaluating score quality.
Always render `rationale_json.notes` as the primary text — this is the
human-readable explanation of why a company scored as it did.
Below notes: list top 3-5 evidence events with title, event_type badge,
severity bar, and event_date.
Below evidence: signals_used counts as small stat chips
(e.g. "12 facilities · 3 regulations · 7 geo events").

### Flag Issue Dialog
A dialog triggered by a "Flag Issue" button in each section of the company detail
**and** by the row-level kebab menu on every reference-data table.

Form: note_type (select: "data_error" | "missing_data" | "outdated" | "other"),
note_text (textarea). Submits to the entity-appropriate POST notes route
(see "Notes / Flag-Issue Pattern" above).

Shows success toast on submit. Notes visible in a collapsible "Flagged Issues"
section at the top of any entity detail page if any open notes exist.

**Generic component (Phase 2):** `components/shared/entity-flag-issue-dialog.tsx`
exports `EntityFlagIssueDialog` accepting:
```ts
type FlaggableEntityType =
  | "company" | "material" | "hs_material_mapping"
  | "regulation" | "risk_event" | "facility" | "battery_chemistry";

interface EntityFlagIssueDialogProps {
  entityType: FlaggableEntityType;
  entityId: string;            // UUIDs and ints both serialized to string
  entityLabel?: string;        // e.g. "Lithium" — shown in dialog header
  sectionLabel?: string;       // optional — prepended to note_text
  trigger?: ReactNode;         // optional custom trigger
}
```
The legacy `components/company/flag-issue-dialog.tsx` becomes a thin wrapper
that calls `EntityFlagIssueDialog` with `entityType="company"`.

### Row Actions Menu
A reusable `components/shared/row-actions-menu.tsx` rendering a `DropdownMenu`
triggered by a `⋯` icon button. Used in the trailing column of every
reference-data table. Always includes a "Flag issue" item that opens the
`EntityFlagIssueDialog`; pages can pass additional menu items as children.

