      { label: "Run Scoring",       href: "/admin/scoring",     icon: Play },
      { label: "Ingestion",         href: "/admin/ingestion",   icon: Download },
      { label: "Seed Review",       href: "/admin/seed-review", icon: ClipboardCheck },
    ]
  }
]
```

---

## API Client Pattern

All API calls go through a single Axios instance that attaches the Clerk JWT.

```ts
// lib/api/client.ts
import axios from 'axios'
import { auth } from '@clerk/nextjs/server'  // server components
// OR
import { useAuth } from '@clerk/nextjs'       // client components

export const apiClient = axios.create({
  baseURL: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL,
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
})

// Interceptor attaches Bearer token on every request
apiClient.interceptors.request.use(async (config) => {
  const token = await getToken()  // from Clerk
  if (token) config.headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`
  return config
})
```

All API functions return typed data. Example:

```ts
// lib/api/companies.ts
export async function getCompanies(params: CompanyListParams): Promise<PaginatedResponse<CompanySummary>> {
  const { data } = await apiClient.get('/api/v1/companies', { params })
  return data
}
```

TanStack Query hooks wrap these:

```ts
// lib/hooks/use-companies.ts
export function useCompanies(params: CompanyListParams) {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: ['companies', params],
    queryFn: () => getCompanies(params),
  })
}
```

---

## Report Generation Flow

This is the most important user flow. Design it carefully.

**Step 1 — /reports/new**
Form with:
- Company selector: searchable multi-select of companies (GET /api/v1/companies to populate)
- Report type: dropdown (Supplier Risk Assessment | Regulatory Compliance | Material Concentration)
- Audience type: dropdown (Internal | OEM Customer | Investor | Public)
- As-of date: date picker (defaults to today)
- Report title: text input (optional, auto-generated if blank)

On submit: POST /api/v1/reports/generate → redirect to /reports/{id}

**Step 2 — /reports/{id}**
Poll GET /api/v1/reports/{id} every 3 seconds while status is queued or running.
Show a progress state while generating.
When completed: render report_insights ordered by sort_order as insight cards.
Show a "Download Report" button that calls GET /api/v1/reports/{id}/download.

**Insight card layout:**
Title (large), insight_type badge (e.g. "MATERIAL RISK" | "REGULATORY FLAG"),
body text (full prose — render as paragraphs, not raw text),
related entity chip if present (company name, material name, or regulation title).

The report viewer should look like a real document, not a dashboard.
Use max-w-3xl centered layout, generous spacing, clear section hierarchy.
A client will read this — it must feel like a professional deliverable.

---

## Scoring Run Flow (Admin)

**Trigger from /admin/scoring page:**
- "Run Scoring" button opens a dialog
- Dialog: optional company filter (all or specific companies), as_of_date
- On confirm: POST /api/v1/scoring/run
- Redirect or show inline status panel
- Poll GET /api/v1/scoring/runs/{run_id} every 5 seconds
- Show progress: "Scoring 45 of 76 companies..."
- On completion: show summary and link to /scores

**Also accessible:** A "Rescore This Company" button on each company score page
that triggers a single-company run without leaving the page.

