NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_...
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_...
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_IN_URL=/login
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_AFTER_SIGN_IN_URL=/dashboard
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# .env (FastAPI additions)
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_...
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000
```

---

## What NOT to Build

- No direct database access from Next.js. All data through FastAPI.
- No client-side data mutation without going through the API.
- No global state management library (Zustand, Redux). TanStack Query handles server
  state. Use React Context only for UI state (sidebar collapse, theme).
- No map visualization yet. Geographic data is displayed as text/tables in Phase 1-4.
- No LLM integration yet. report_insights.body is pre-populated by the backend.
- No real-time WebSocket connections. Polling is sufficient for run status.
- No chart library beyond shadcn/ui charts (which wraps Recharts). Do not install
  Tremor — it does not support React 19. Do not install Chart.js, Victory, Nivo,
  or any other visualization library. If shadcn/ui charts don't cover a use case,
  reconsider whether the visualization is necessary.